A||||1||the need for speed||puting on koni shocks and eibach springs need a little help||||1||
Z||000000||the need for speed||10-23-2000||01:50 AM||||Am installing koni shocks with eibach springs, I have got the spring on the shock (like the one that came off), but it does not seem tight enough, I can wiggle & turn the spring a little. On the other one, I put the  metal plate (flat plate with center cone and 3 holes for bolts that attach to car) on upside down, and the spring is tighter and doesn't wiggle or turn as much like the old shock and spring.  Is there anything else to do to tighten the spring or am I suppose to turn the plate upside down.||||reg||1
Z||000001||BAM-BAM||10-23-2000||07:51 AM||||  That is a normal anomaly. It's the same with the KYB struts (you are talking about the rear). Once they are on the car they will seat fine and never unseat untill you raise the vehical. What I did was (and this came from the Forum) drilled three 3/16" holes in the side ot the strut cap, not the flat plate, but the part that is beveled, directly below the existing holes. These holes corresponded in location with the existing holes. After the cap nut was tight, I put pressure on the strut cap to compress the whole assymbely and the ran safety wire through the holes and around the spring and pulled it tight then tied it off. There is also a small, single hole in the bottom seat, tie this off first. That will hold the assymbely together tightly.<BR>You might want some one to help you, it gets a little awkward at times. The reason this happens is because the stut plunger is designed for the stock spring and it is longer than the lowering spring. Therefore, you have slop. It would be nice if Eibach contracted with KONI or KYB to have  the strut plungers modified. But then you would probably oay half again as much and KONI's are already expensive enough. I hope this helps you a little. If not, then be patient other will be here to help.<P>  Later, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT<BR>Eibach Springs/KYB shocks and struts<BR>Mr.Mikes 500 series seats, Carpet and headliner! YEAH BABY-YEAH||||reg||12
